  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "The interval $x\\in (-14,\\infty )$ corresponds to the inequality",
  "worked_solution": "The statement $x\\in (-14,\\infty )$ means that $x$ lies between $-14$ and $\\infty ,$ where \n\n- the left endpoint $-14$ is *not* included, and\n\n- the right endpoint $\\infty $ is *not* included.\n\nTherefore, the inequality represented by this interval is \n\n$$\n-14<x<\\infty .\n$$\n\nHowever, since all numbers are smaller than infinity, it suffices to write \n\n$$\n-14<x\n$$\n\nor, equivalently, \n\n$$\nx>-14.\n$$",
